==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*4 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[St. Dober]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Chickful A]] spawns.
**1 [[Othom]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage introduces St. Dober, who is like Dober P.D, except with every weakness removed. He's faster, stronger, and can't be CC'd by anti-Traitless units like Tourist or Crystal. To prevent him from getting walled by [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] like every other Angel, Relic enemies appear here to Curse your meatshields, giving St. Dober complete rein to kill all of your units as he sees fit. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] stacking is your best way out here.

Once you stack two Cyberpunk Cats, lure St. Dober to the base and beat Othom up fast. Combinations of [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] are recommended here for Othom. Once that's done, chip Dober down using units like Ramen Cat, [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], and a Surge Immune unit. At this point in the game, your only Surge Immune backliner will probably be [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]], so use him as backliner damage. Feel free to swap him out with either [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] or a suitable Surge Immune Uber, though.

On future clears of this stage, you'll probaly have both [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]], who combined completely obliterate this stage.

